 "notes": "The list starts near the foot of p. 63 (n70.jpg), rows 81–90, and ends on p. 64 (n71.jpg), rows 91–115. n68 (p. 61, East Coast of England), n69 and n72 don't have it. No 'L.H.'/'L.V.' types and no light characters are printed. The last column is the height in feet: the first row on each page reads 'ft.' and the rows below use ',,' (ditto) for it. In the 'printed' field I wrote the dot leaders as '....' and didn't keep their exact lengths. The asterisk columns under '79 '80 '81 '82 '83 almost certainly mean the years each station sent returns. The text above the list says schedules went to 34 stations and returns came from 17. That fits: there are 34 numbers (81–115 with no 106), and exactly 17 rows have an asterisk under '83. In 'marks' I gave the asterisks with the year columns they sit under, judged by their position on the page.\n\nDitto marks for places: rows 82 (Rhu Stoir) and 112–114 (Loch Ryan, Portpatrick, Mull of Galloway) print ',,' where the county would be. These mean Sutherland and Wigtonshire. I kept ',,' as printed in 'place'.\n\nBrace rows: nos. 93 (Hynish Signal Tower, Tyree) and 94 (Skerryvore, off Tyree) share one brace. The five asterisks, the height '150 ,,' and the keeper 'Wm. Crow' all go with the brace. I gave both rows the same 'printed' line. Hynish was the shore station for Skerryvore. At no. 86, Monach Isles, two heights (150 and 62) are braced together against one keeper. The Monach Isles had two lights, so these are probably their two heights. The keeper is printed 'J.Youngclause', with no space. The General Remarks that follow call him 'Mr. James Youngclause, Monach lighthouse'.\n\nSpellings copied as printed: 'Kircudbright' (for Kirkcudbright); 'Lochindaul' (Loch Indaal); 'Rhuvaal'; 'Skervuile'; 'Dhuheartach' (usually Dubh Artach); 'Ushenish'; 'Rosshire'; 'Wigtonshire'; 'Argyl.'; 'Tyree'. 'M‘' is printed with a turned comma (M‘Culloch, M‘Lellan, M‘Arthur's).\n\nSpacing: the type is set tight in 'J.Youngclause', 'Robt.Laidlaw', 'Corran Ferry,Loch Eil' and 'Little Ross,Kircudbright', so I left out the space. This is probably just the printer fitting the line, not a meaningful difference.\n\nNo. 92 prints 'Ardnamurchan Pt.|Argyl.' with a vertical stroke where a comma would be expected. It is probably a damaged sort.\n\nNo. 90 (Kyleakin): I read the height as 53; the OCR has 58.\n\nUnnumbered tail: nos. 116, 117, 118, '119 [1880]' and 120 are printed with nothing after the numbers (only '[1880]' after 119), so I left them out as you asked. The General Remarks then begin with Youngclause (Monach) and William Irvine (Barra Head: 'the first report I have received'). That fits Barra Head having an asterisk under '83 only.\n\nThe OCR errors I corrected from the images include: '108. Bhinne of Iglavs' = 103. Rhinns of Islay; '118. Portpatrick' = 113; 'Polat: GiaSS' = 85. Island Glass; 'Wahenteh' = 87. Ushenish; 'Mull of Kintyvre' = Kintyre (297 ft); 'Pladda … Teo' = 130; Mull of Galloway '3825' = 325.",
